  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="86b5a281-40b8-5f5f-85de-b6029f4420c3" activityNameId="0cf60f06-5395-515f-9f5c-408e01875a72" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">xxx Operation, long-distance train, SBB mix</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: xxx Operation, long-distance train, SBB mix
Average data for the operation of Swiss long distance trains (Intercity, Eurocity, CIS/ICE/TGV, Interregio, and Express trains). The data has been determined top down, by combining the total yearly energy consumption and the yearly tkm-performance of long-distance transportation of the SBB. Particulate emissions due to abrasion of rail tracks, wheels, brakes and overhead contact line is included. Emission of sulphur hexafluoride (SF6) occurring during conversion at traction substations are accounted for. For a first estimate of European long distance trains, the user may change the electricity mix.;
UUID: 6551952a-2a4c-32c1-9f43-460e1232de57
The inventory includes the actual energy consumption due to traction.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: all technologies included
Time period: all data is based on situation in the year 2000, except the specific energy consumption per pkm (year 2008)
Production volume: 8522 Mio pkm in 2000  in Switzerland
Sampling: SBB studies and own assumptions 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6551952a-2a4c-32c1-9f43-460e1232de57.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
